aster","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-6507](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-6507)\r\n### Description\n\nAs part of the fix for https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/12554, we introduced a map in consumer tablet to generate the write_id for multiple updates in each transaction. This map is only cleared when there are transaction updates present in the same batch as transaction apply; in other cases, this map will continuously build up over time and use a bunch of memory. In ad-hoc testing we found that in some cases we have close 2.3m entries being tracked in this map.\n\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\n\n- [X] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\n\n[DB-6507]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-6507?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/17276/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/17276/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]